1
00:00:00,593 --> 00:00:03,403
Hi! This tutorial shows two static tricks

2
00:00:03,887 --> 00:00:08,046
to help you get used to the unicycle
before you even know how to ride.

3
00:00:09,357 --> 00:00:12,476
The first trick is standing on the frame.

4
00:00:13,337 --> 00:00:16,848
Find a place where you can hold on,
and get on the unicycle.

5
00:00:17,666 --> 00:00:22,143
Put both feet at the same height,
with the cranks parallel to the ground.

6
00:00:23,027 --> 00:00:25,456
I turn in the video so you can see better,

7
00:00:25,643 --> 00:00:28,852
but try to stay upright,
holding on to the wall with one hand.

8
00:00:29,929 --> 00:00:33,332
Once you're stable,
take your foot off the front pedal.

9
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:37,310
Next, place it on the wheel,
with your heel on the frame

10
00:00:37,354 --> 00:00:38,670
and your toes on the tire.

11
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:42,681
Press down a little
with your foot to lock the wheel.

12
00:00:44,056 --> 00:00:47,433
Then lift your other foot
and place it on the frame.

13
00:00:48,084 --> 00:00:50,194
That foot doesn't need to touch the tire.

14
00:00:52,371 --> 00:00:56,553
In this position, most of your weight
should be on the saddle.

15
00:00:58,331 --> 00:01:02,309
Next, grab the saddle and pull the handle

16
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:05,059
while pushing with your legs
to stand up.

17
00:01:05,793 --> 00:01:07,982
Always keep a little pressure

18
00:01:08,013 --> 00:01:12,029
on your toes to lock the wheel,
or the unicycle will move.

19
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:18,900
To get back down, grab the saddle
without leaning too far forward,

20
00:01:19,284 --> 00:01:21,505
pull the handle, and sit down.

21
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:27,030
Then put your other foot
back on the rear pedal,

22
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:30,869
and bit by bit,
take the pressure off your toes.

23
00:01:31,437 --> 00:01:35,936
Now the foot on the rear pedal
keeps you balanced.

24
00:01:38,117 --> 00:01:40,986
There you go, you're back
in the starting position.

25
00:01:42,747 --> 00:01:46,128
The second trick is to sit on the tire.

26
00:01:46,658 --> 00:01:49,687
To do this, start
in the same position as before:

27
00:01:49,991 --> 00:01:53,046
pedals at the same height,
cranks parallel to the ground.

28
00:01:54,873 --> 00:01:58,585
Straighten your legs to lift your butt,
and let go of the saddle.

29
00:01:59,208 --> 00:02:02,256
Pull the handle
to bring the saddle out in front of you.

30
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:04,269
Slide your hand to place it

31
00:02:04,293 --> 00:02:09,060
in the middle of the saddle,
which helps you control it better.

32
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:12,585
Pull the saddle against you
and bend your knees

33
00:02:12,622 --> 00:02:14,463
until you touch the tire.

34
00:02:14,663 --> 00:02:16,808
Once you're comfortable in this position,

35
00:02:17,018 --> 00:02:20,870
put the saddle on the ground
by sliding your hand along the frame.

36
00:02:20,927 --> 00:02:26,357
[Music]

37
00:02:26,423 --> 00:02:29,771
Pick up the saddle
by sliding your hand along the frame.

38
00:02:29,875 --> 00:02:33,582
Hold the saddle firmly
and press it against your chest.

39
00:02:33,830 --> 00:02:35,192
Then you can get back on.

40
00:02:35,996 --> 00:02:38,409
Straighten your legs
and pull the saddle in.

41
00:02:38,433 --> 00:02:44,102
[Music]

42
00:02:44,873 --> 00:02:49,269
You can try these tricks with your feet
on the pedals or on the cranks.

43
00:02:49,893 --> 00:02:53,962
You might feel more stable
on the cranks at first.

44
00:02:55,087 --> 00:02:56,087
Have a good session!

45
00:02:56,150 --> 00:03:03,240
[Music]

